# Dependencies (installed fresh inside the build)
**/node_modules

# Build outputs (rebuilt inside the build)
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/coverage

# TypeScript incremental build bookkeeping. If CI's own `pnpm build` step
# (which runs before the Docker build steps, on the same checkout) has
# already compiled a package, this file exists but the `dist/` it refers to
# is excluded above — tsc's incremental compiler trusts this file's record
# of "already compiled" without verifying the output actually exists, and
# silently skips re-emitting, which starves the next package's `tsc` of the
# type declarations it needs. Confirmed directly: this exact sequence caused
# `apps/api`'s Docker build to fail with "Cannot find module
# '@platform/logger'" even though the source was correct.
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Version control
.git

# Environment / secrets — never bake these into an image layer
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Editor / OS
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Turbo's own prune output, if generated locally
out
